# Line endings for the deployment artifacts (F5).
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which means a
# fresh clone materialises text files with CRLF in the working tree. Copying a
# CRLF shell script to the VDS produces one of the least helpful errors in
# existence: `$'\r': command not found`, pointing at a line that looks correct.
# The same applies to a Caddyfile fragment pasted into the shared configuration.
#
# Deliberately narrow: no `* text=auto` catch-all, so nothing here changes how
# the Flutter client's or the backend's source files are checked out.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
Caddyfile* text eol=lf
*.sudoers text eol=lf
*.env.example text eol=lf

# Read only by tools that accept either ending, but keeping them LF means the
# compose file the server sees is byte-identical to the one CI validated. Scoped
# to these paths rather than `*.yaml` so that nothing under app/ changes.
/.github/workflows/*.yml text eol=lf
/compose.prod.yaml text eol=lf
/deploy/*.yaml text eol=lf

# PowerShell backup scripts stay on the Windows convention: they only ever run
# on the machine that pulls the backups.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
